   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## kubakub director · h3 clips\n\nMiniMax H3 generates **video with sound** for stretches of the director's timeline. The director renders every\nframe; H3 replaces the stretch of each **keyframe clip**. It starts on the director's frame at the clip start\nand ends on the frame at the clip end, so the lamps, layers and masks around the clip stay exact.\n\n1. Queue once: the scene renders and the regions appear; H3 waits until you apply (director flow: hold until apply).\n2. **Open director**. In the timeline:\n   - **H3 clips** → add a clip, write what happens (\"gold light runs up the arches\"), optionally a sound.\n   - Markers (**M**) inside a clip with a **name** become beats in the prompt (\"[1s-2s] …\").\n   - Tick **pin frames** for a marker in the clip popup (a diamond appears on the marker): H3 also passes\n     through the director's picture at that moment. Use it to force a look in the middle of a clip.\n   - A **reference** clip uses the director's stretch as the motion reference (ref2va, 8 steps).\n3. **Apply** (it queues). **Director sequence** (3b) renders the frames; skip_h3_frames on: it skips the frames H3 replaces (except the pinned ones and\n   the crossfade frames). The 9B enhancer writes the H3 prompt (about 9 s), see \"the prompts h3 got\".\n4. For delivery: un-bypass node 5 (ctrl b), pick ProRes 422 HQ / 4444 (alpha) / PNG / H.264 HQ;\n   it writes to output/kubakub_export. Director sequence (3b) can export its frames without H3 (export widget).\n\nVRAM: H3 needs about 11.5 GB. Unload other models first (Manager → unload models).\nA 2 s clip at 0.85 MP, 4 steps takes about a minute on the 5070 Ti. Re-runs of unchanged clips are cached.\n"
   ],
   "title": "read me"
  }
